---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageLead from "../components/PageLead.astro";
import ArrowIcon from "../components/ArrowIcon.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="AnalyseSpider changelog"
  description="Public record of user-visible changes, limits, and release state for the new AnalyseSpider implementation."
  canonicalPath="/changelog"
>
  <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Changelog</span></nav>
  <PageLead
    title="Changes that affect what you can inspect or trust"
    intro="A public record of user-visible tools, content, evidence boundaries, and release state. Internal plumbing stays out unless it changes the result."
    index="71"
  />
  <section class="change-log" aria-label="Changelog entries">
    <article>
      <div class="change-date"><time datetime="2026-08-27">27 AUG 2026</time><span>LIVE URL CHECK</span></div>
      <div>
        <h2>One protected crawler check with four plain answers</h2>
        <p>Added a bilingual live URL check for fetch access, search-crawler access, indexability, and server-visible main content. The result exposes technical evidence without turning it into a synthetic visibility score.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The operation uses one concurrent slot, 30 runs per 24 hours per pseudonymous client, and no paid SEO or LLM provider.</li>
          <li>The public-tools container is capped at 0.5 CPU and 256 MB, separate from the Contextter Site Audit worker.</li>
          <li>Privacy, methodology, sitemap, CSP, internal links, and common-owner disclosures now match the live data path.</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="text-link" href="/tools/crawler-view">Open the crawler check <ArrowIcon /></a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <div class="change-date"><time datetime="2026-08-23">23 AUG 2026</time><span>PLAIN LANGUAGE</span></div>
      <div>
        <h2>Simpler design, bilingual entry pages and crawler comparison</h2>
        <p>Reorganised the site around three clear jobs: use a tool, understand a crawling question or compare crawler systems. Replaced the heavy display style with a readable system sans-serif and a lighter visual hierarchy.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Added German entry pages for the home, tools, crawler and knowledge areas.</li>
          <li>Added a primary-source comparison of search and AI crawler roles without naming an unsupported product winner.</li>
          <li>Related Fan-out links appear only in relevant sections with common ownership visible; no Contextter product link was added.</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="text-link" href="/crawlers">Compare crawler systems <ArrowIcon /></a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <div class="change-date"><time datetime="2026-08-22">22 AUG 2026</time><span>CHAIN EVIDENCE</span></div>
      <div>
        <h2>Redirect chain evidence and crawler verification comparison</h2>
        <p>Replaced the interim redirect-chain alias with a dedicated browser-local chain builder, executable parsing fixtures, and structured evidence output. Added a primary-source comparison of crawler verification methods.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Relative Location fields, capture gaps, loops, and incomplete final states stay visible.</li>
          <li>No tool fetches a URL or verifies a crawler identity on the visitor's behalf.</li>
          <li>The log inspector can now export aggregate evidence without the raw log lines.</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="text-link" href="/tools/redirect-chain">Open the chain builder <ArrowIcon /></a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <div class="change-date"><time datetime="2026-08-22">22 AUG 2026</time><span>EVIDENCE RELEASE</span></div>
      <div>
        <h2>Robots rule testing and executed fixtures</h2>
        <p>Added a browser-local RFC 9309 rule tester, a reproducible testing guide, and seven versioned fixtures whose expected decisions run during build verification.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The tool performs no network request and does not claim crawler-vendor parity.</li>
          <li>The benchmark page now publishes actual local fixture outcomes instead of a protocol-only placeholder.</li>
          <li>The repository records one primary job for every indexable canonical URL.</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="text-link" href="/tools/robots-rule-tester">Open the robots tester <ArrowIcon /></a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <div class="change-date"><time datetime="2026-08-22">22 AUG 2026</time><span>PUBLIC LAUNCH</span></div>
      <div>
        <h2>Canonical pages released for indexing</h2>
        <p>Removed the coordinated metadata, response-header, and robots blocking signals after the owner-approved minimum viable launch passed legal, legacy URL, sitemap, responsive, and production checks.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The sitemap is generated from the canonical route and content registries and contains only indexable 200 pages.</li>
          <li>The `www` host permanently preserves paths while redirecting to the canonical apex.</li>
          <li>Tool, guide, reference, and article schema now describes the visible page role.</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="text-link" href="/sitemap.xml">Inspect the sitemap <ArrowIcon /></a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <div class="change-date"><time datetime="2026-08-22">22 AUG 2026</time><span>LEGAL</span></div>
      <div>
        <h2>Operator and privacy boundary published</h2>
        <p>Added the verified legal operator details and a technology-specific privacy notice covering Vercel request delivery, browser-local tool processing, email contact, external links, and data-subject rights.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>No analytics, advertising tags, accounts, or contact form are currently active.</li>
          <li>Tool input and results stay in the visitor's browser; hosting request metadata remains a separate infrastructure boundary.</li>
          <li>The acquired-domain ownership and rights separation remains explicit.</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="text-link" href="/privacy">Read the privacy notice <ArrowIcon /></a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <div class="change-date"><time datetime="2026-08-22">22 AUG 2026</time><span>PRE-LAUNCH</span></div>
      <div>
        <h2>Diagnostic library and responsive type hardening</h2>
        <p>Added dedicated Tools, Guides, Lab Notes, Reference, and audience hubs. Published four diagnostic guides, three primary-source reference pages, three dated lab notes, About, and this changelog.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Large headings wrap inside their grid track instead of being clipped by fixed sidebar widths or no-wrap rules.</li>
          <li>Navigation, content rows, tables, source links, and technical strings have explicit narrow-screen behavior.</li>
          <li>This release remained noindex until the later public-launch gate passed.</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="text-link" href="/guides">Inspect the guide library <ArrowIcon /></a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <div class="change-date"><time datetime="2026-08-22">22 AUG 2026</time><span>FOUNDATION</span></div>
      <div>
        <h2>Three browser-local inspectors</h2>
        <p>Introduced a bounded access-log parser, a paste-only HTTP response and HTML inspector, and a local IP syntax and reserved-range check.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>No current tool uploads submitted data.</li>
          <li>No current tool fetches an arbitrary URL or scans a target.</li>
          <li>Results distinguish observations, inferences, and unknowns.</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="text-link" href="/tools">Open the tools index <ArrowIcon /></a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <div class="change-date"><time datetime="2026-08-22">22 AUG 2026</time><span>RIGHTS</span></div>
      <div>
        <h2>New ownership and legacy URL decisions</h2>
        <p>Published the new-ownership boundary and URL-level decisions for the strongest historical targets. No former software, content, customers, or operator identity is presented as transferred.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/legacy">Read the legacy map <ArrowIcon /></a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
